2 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K (32 threads) - 63.71 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nStarting with 4.7.rc2, the engine seems to fail to load random textures in my 2D (D3D12, Forward+) project. The failing textures are not always the same ones. This occurs both in editor and exported. Deleting the .godot folder to force a re-import does not help. See below for the same scene in 4.7.rc1 (good) vs 4.7.rc2 (bad). If you are unable to repro it, I can share the project privately (@hpvb has a copy).\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/06cd3693-ae84-4dc5-928a-e8e8e30828c2\" />\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4b99ecb2-fb6a-4292-9d11-6f6ba06eefb0\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open an affected project in the editor.\n- Hit Play.\n- Observe that most of the time the screen is full of magenta placeholder textures.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nUnable to repro in a small project.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repi